; lang.xon -- what this bundle IS.
;
; xon: read with the ordinary reader and never evaluated, like every other
; manifest in the x-lang world (pin.xon, engine.pin.xon).  A form a reader
; does not know is a loud error, never a skip -- a manifest that silently
; ignores half of itself cannot be extended without wondering which readers
; obeyed which half.
;
; FORMAT (one form per line):
;   (lang "NAME")               the -l name
;   (dialect NAME)              he | xe | rn -- a REQUIREMENT, not a taste
;   (requires-release "TAG")    the x-lang this bundle was built against
;   (entry "FILE")              loaded AFTER the dialect, not instead of it

(lang "krn")

; HELIUM, and this is derived rather than preferred.  Kernel's imports are
; krn/base and krn/printer; neither reaches past x-core -- no float, no
; socket, no file.  Declaring a heavier dialect would be a lie that costs
; every user a numeric tower they never call.
(dialect he)

; NO PAIRING ROW YET, and the absence is deliberate rather than an oversight.
; This row names the x-lang release a bundle was built against, compared for
; EQUALITY and never parsed.  No released x-lang can run this bundle: bundle
; acquisition, `-l` loading, --share-dir and eval!-in-the-seam all landed after
; v0.5.2, which is still the latest tag.  Declaring v0.5.2 would name a
; platform that answers "Unknown option: --share-dir"; declaring a tag that
; does not exist would be a promise, not a fact.
;
; So it says nothing, Pin bundle reports "platform pairing unchecked", and that
; is the honest state.  Add the row -- and the same string to the CI matrix,
; they are one fact -- when x-lang cuts a release carrying the machinery.

(entry "run.x")
